
class prompts:
    sys_prompt = "You are a journalist tasked with rating the political bias of articles submitted to you based only on the topics, you will be especially focused on omission bias, that is bias created by leaving out information or talking points when discussing a piece of news.\n[OUTPUT FORMAT]\nOutput in JSON format as per the following example:\n{bias:<your bias classification>}\n Only choose from one category and only include the category name with no thinking text. USE ONLY BRITISH ENGLISH SPELLING."
    user_prompt = "The article is enclosed with the <article> xml tags. Given the article, analyze the political bias focusing on omission bias as defined in the system prompt. The article's format is as follows: <site> | <title> | <article text>. \n Classify the article into one of the following categories: 'left', 'leaning-left', 'center', 'leaning-right','right'. Only classify it into one category and do not include anything other than the category name in the response JSON."
    topics_sys_prompt = "You are a research assistant specialized in content analysis. Your task is to analyze a given article and compare it against similar articles on the same topic found via web search.\nYou must follow these rules strictly:\n\n- Return EXACTLY two numbered lists, no more, no less.\n- Each list contains EXACTLY 5 talking points — never fewer, never more.\n- Each talking point is one concise sentence (max 10 words) and omit all references and associated formatting, return only the talking point itself without any '[1]' references.\n- Do not include introductions, summaries, explanations, headers beyond the two list titles, or any other text.\n- Do not combine or split points to game the count.\n\nOutput is as follows:\n{'covered':[topic1,topic2,...]\n,'omitted':[topic1,topic2,...]}\n DO NOT INCLUDE ANYTHING OUTSIDE OF THE ABOVE STRUCTURE, ONLY INCLUDE THE ABOVE JSON IN THE OUTPUT."
    topics_user_prompt = "Search the web for articles similar to the one below, then analyze both the article and the similar articles you find.\n\nReturn exactly:\n- 5 talking points that are covered in the article below\n- 5 talking points that appear in similar articles but are NOT covered in the article below\n\nNothing else. No extra text.\nThe article is below within the <article> tags. with the following format. <site (news channel that authored the article)> | <title> | <article text>"